@page "/kanban/stacked-header"

@using Syncfusion.Blazor.KanbanDemo
@using Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban
@*Hidden:Lines*@
@inherits SampleBaseComponent;
@*End:Hidden*@

<ActionDescription>
<p>
    This sample demonstrates the <a class="e-kanban-stackedheader-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the explore Syncfusion Blazor Kanban component"
                                                                                                        href="https://www.syncfusion.com/gantt-sdk/blazor-kanban-board"
                                                                                                        target="_blank" rel="noopener">Blazor Kanban</a> component with the stacked header feature by visualizing a Assembly Line Tasks. The board displays two headers aligned in a stacked manner so the workflow phases are visually grouped.
</p>
<p>
    Add an additional header above column headers to group related columns. Configure stacked headers by mapping <a class="e-kanban-stackedheader-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the API reference of Text property in Kanban"
                                                                                                        href="https://help.syncfusion.com/cr/blazor/Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban.KanbanStackedHeader.html#Syncfusion_Blazor_Kanban_KanbanStackedHeader_Text"
                                                                                                        target="_blank" rel="noopener">Text</a> and <a class="e-kanban-stackedheader-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the API reference of KeyFields property in Kanban"
                                                                                                        href="https://help.syncfusion.com/cr/blazor/Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban.KanbanStackedHeader.html#Syncfusion_Blazor_Kanban_KanbanStackedHeader_KeyFields"
                                                                                                        target="_blank" rel="noopener">KeyFields</a> in the <a class="e-kanban-stackedheader-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the API reference of KanbanStackedHeader"
                                                                                                        href="https://help.syncfusion.com/cr/blazor/Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban.KanbanStackedHeader.html"
                                                                                                        target="_blank" rel="noopener">KanbanStackedHeader</a> collection.
</p>
<p>
    Additional essential interactions that enhance analysis and control are also featured:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <a aria-label="Navigate to the documentation for the stacked header in the kanban component"
           href="https://blazor.syncfusion.com/documentation/kanban/columns#stacked-headers"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Stacked Header</a>: Add a second header row that groups related columns into logical phases.
    </li>
    <li>
        <a aria-label="Navigate to the documentation for the columns in the kanban component"
           href="https://blazor.syncfusion.com/documentation/kanban/columns"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Columns</a>: Group cards by workflow stage such as Open, In Progress, In Review, and Completed.
    </li>
    <li>
        <a aria-label="Navigate to the documentation for the tooltip in the kanban component"
           href="https://blazor.syncfusion.com/documentation/kanban/tooltip"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tooltip</a>: Show extra card details on hover to surface context without cluttering the card.
    </li>
</ul>
<p>
    Key interactive features demonstrated in this sample include:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>Phase Groups</b>: Columns are grouped into logical phases such as To Do, Development Phase, and Done via the stacked header.</li>
    <li><b>Custom Stacked Text</b>: Each stacked header renders a custom label that describes the workflow phase.</li>
    <li><b>Column Mapping</b>: The <code>KeyFields</code> of a stacked header map the columns that should fall under that group.</li>
    <li><b>Tooltip Support</b>: Cards display a tooltip on hover for quick access to additional details.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    The <b>Stacked Header Configuration</b> highlights the building blocks of a custom stacked layout:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>Text</b>: The label rendered in the stacked header row.</li>
    <li><b>KeyFields</b>: The list of column key fields grouped under the stacked header.</li>
    <li><b>KanbanStackedHeaders</b>: The collection of stacked headers rendered above the column headers.</li>
</ul>
<p>
Looking for the full Blazor Kanban component overview, features, pricing, and documentation? Visit the <a class="e-kanban-stackedheader-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the explore Syncfusion Blazor Kanban component" href="https://www.syncfusion.com/gantt-sdk/blazor-kanban-board" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Blazor Kanban</a> page.</p>
</ActionDescription>


<div class="col-lg-12 control-section">
    <SfKanban KeyField="Status" DataSource="@CardData" EnableTooltip="true" Height="500px">
        <KanbanColumns>
            @foreach (ColumnModel item in ColumnData)
            {
                <KanbanColumn HeaderText="@item.HeaderText" KeyField="@item.KeyField"/>
            }
        </KanbanColumns>
        <KanbanCardSettings ContentField="Summary" HeaderField="Id">
            <Template>
                @{
                    KanbanDataModel card = (KanbanDataModel)context;
                    <div class="stacked-card" style="border-left-color: @card.Color;">
                        <div class="sc-header">
                            <span class="sc-id">@card.Id</span>
                            <span class="sc-priority" data-priority="@card.Priority">
                                <span class="sc-priority-dot"></span>
                                @card.Priority
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(card.Title))
                        {
                            <div class="sc-title">@card.Title</div>
                        }
                        <div class="sc-content">@card.Summary</div>
                        <div class="sc-tags">
                            @if (card.CardTags != null)
                            {
                                @foreach (string tag in card.CardTags)
                                {
                                    <span class="sc-tag">@tag</span>
                                }
                            }
                        </div>
                        <div class="sc-footer">
                            <div class="sc-type">
                                <span class="sc-type-icon"></span>
                                <span>@card.Type</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="sc-assignee">
                                <span class="sc-avatar" style="background: @card.Color;">
                                    @GetInitials(card.Assignee)
                                </span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
            </Template>
        </KanbanCardSettings>
        <KanbanStackedHeaders>
            @foreach (StackedHeaderModel item in StackedHeaderData)
            {
                <KanbanStackedHeader Text="@item.Text" KeyFields="@item.KeyFields"/>
            }
        </KanbanStackedHeaders>
    </SfKanban>
</div>
